B.bld=s(["The fetus is covered in fine hair (lanugo), has some scalp hair, and is capable of producing IgG and IgM (two types of antibodies).","The parathyroid begins to regulate calcium metabolism.","The adrenal are starting to produce significant levels of cortisol.","The average fetus at 20 weeks is 10.1 inches (25.7 cm) long and weighs 11.7 ounces (331 grams)."],t.s)
